# CK1 — boot the HG-UV98 reconstruction to a running OS tick (canonical run).
#
# Session-45 state: boot chain verified (Reset_Handler → SystemInit → main →
# OSInit → 7 tasks → OSStart → context switches), and the SysTick→OS tick
# chain verified end-to-end. Root cause of the session-44 "silent tick" was
# NEVER a delivery problem — see the session-45 log entry:
#   1) The vendored Micrium port's OS_CPU_SysTickInit (ucos2/port/os_cpu_c.c)
#      never writes SYST_CVR: RVR=cnts-1, SHPRI3, then two CSR read-modify-
#      writes (|=CLKSOURCE|ENABLE, |=TICKINT).
#   2) Renode models SysTick as a descending LimitTimer whose CURRENT=0 view
#      (CVR never written) counts from the 24-bit limit, so the first
#      LimitReached lands at 0xFFFFFF/systickFrequency (≈156 ms @108 MHz,
#      ≈233 ms @72 MHz) — past every session-44 observation window.
#   3) Silicon wraps CVR=0 to LOAD+1 on the next edge (≈1 ms), so this is a
#      Renode-vs-silicon divergence, NOT a firmware bug.
# Workaround (harness-side only, permitted by the mission rules; must be
# restated in every equivalence report): after boot, write SYST_CVR=0 from
# the monitor — the app's own RVR then takes effect on the first underflow
# and the tick runs at the app's intended 1 kHz.

using sysbus
mach create "hguv98"

# Project platform: stock stm32f103.repl with systickFrequency = 108 MHz
# (the firmware's HCLK assumption; the stock 72 MHz made ticks 1.5 ms).
machine LoadPlatformDescription @/home/sslayer/Proyectos/HG-UV98/reconstruction/sim/gd32f103.repl

# bootloader-equivalent vector handoff (the app is linked at 0x08004000
# behind the non-distributed bootloader; it sets VTOR itself in main)
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00000000 0x20006800
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00000004 0x08004165

# SystemInit selects PLL then polls CFGR SCLK_STS; the tag makes it "done"
sysbus Tag <0x40021004, 0x40021007> "RCC_CFGR" 0x00000008

sysbus LoadELF @/home/sslayer/Proyectos/HG-UV98/reconstruction/build/hguv98.elf

# protocol UART output (USART2) to the console
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2

echo "=== boot 10 ms ==="
emulation RunFor "00:00:00.010"

# harness-side CVR workaround (see header)
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0xE000E018 0x00000000

echo "=== run 100 ms — OS tick @1 kHz ==="
emulation RunFor "00:00:00.100"
echo "=== OSCtxSwCtr (0x200020BC; boot-only was <10):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x200020BC
echo "=== OSIdleCtr (0x20001FE0; >0 means idle got CPU time):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20001FE0

echo "=== run 100 ms more ==="
emulation RunFor "00:00:00.100"
echo "=== OSCtxSwCtr again (must have grown ~100):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x200020BC
echo "=== OSIdleCtr again:"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20001FE0
echo "=== fault registers (must stay 0):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0xE000ED28
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0xE000ED2C
quit
